The VA funding fee is a one-time charge of 1.25% to 3.3% of the loan amount, typically rolled into the loan balance. It funds the VA guarantee program so it costs taxpayers nothing. Veterans with a service-connected disability rating of 10% or higher are completely exempt, saving $4,375 to $11,550 on a typical $350,000 loan. Purple Heart recipients and surviving spouses of veterans who died in service or from a service-connected disability are also exempt. On a purchase loan, the [VA funding fee schedule](https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/funding-fee-and-closing-costs/) sets the rate by down payment: 2.15% on first use (3.3% after first use) with less than 5% down, 1.5% with 5% to under 10% down, and 1.25% with 10% or more down. Each rate is a percent of the loan amount, so it is charged on what you borrow after the down payment rather than on the home's purchase price.